# FLIXO Release Product Directive

FLIXO exposes two supported workflows for the certified browser-local image capabilities:

1. Agent Guided Workflow — the user supplies an image and a natural-language instruction. A deterministic local planner resolves the request against the canonical executable registry, produces a bounded execution plan, and requires explicit user confirmation before execution.
2. Manual Standalone Workflow — the user opens a tool route and executes the operation directly.

Release boundaries:
- Image processing remains browser-local.
- Raw File/Blob bytes never enter the agent request contract and are never sent to an LLM/provider/backend.
- Agent execution is limited to the canonical executable capability set, one local step at a time, with fail-closed output verification.
- The canonical registry remains authoritative for capability state, schemas, execution mode, safety requirements, recovery policy, executor binding, and output contract.
- Non-executable or ambiguous requests fail closed and remain available through the manual tool surface when appropriate.
- Production deployment remains the Cloudflare Workers exact-SHA pipeline defined in CI.
